From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:54:50 +0200
Subject: nv30: on the PS3, no submission ends inside an indexed draw's
 primitive

The re-review of 0073 (M1'): a plain indexed draw reserved only its binding and BEGIN, so the
batches' own space check could still end the submission inside the primitive. ps3rsx then copies
the binding on to the index buffer's end (up to 1 MiB) and counts that against the submission's
share of its ring, on top of what Mesa counted: with about 0.25 MiB already in the submission it is
refused. A plain draw under the cap now reserves all of its words before its binding, as a piece
does (binding, BEGIN, batches, END: at most about 2.06k words), so a flush falls only before an
indexed draw. A draw past the cap that couldn't be split keeps the binding-and-BEGIN reservation.

L7: the space check is now inline (PUSH_AVAIL first, as PUSH_SPACE does): a draw with room in the
push buffer makes no call into the winsys and takes no lock, as before 0073. Draws send the same
words as before 0072 wherever no flush was due.

Forwarded: no

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_vbo.c b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_vbo.c
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_vbo.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_vbo.c
@@ -578,7 +578,9 @@ nv30_idx_binding_room(struct nv30_context *nv30, uint64_t copy, unsigned words)
    struct nouveau_pushbuf *push = nv30->base.pushbuf;
    struct nouveau_device *dev = nv30->screen->base.device;
 
-   PUSH_SPACE_EX(push, words + 8, 2, 0);
+   /* (inline, as PUSH_SPACE: with room, as nearly always, no call and no lock) */
+   if (PUSH_AVAIL(push) < words + 8)
+      PUSH_SPACE_EX(push, words + 8, 2, 0);
    if (nv30->ps3_idx_bytes && nv30->ps3_idx_bytes + copy > NV30_PS3_IDX_SUBMIT_BYTES) {
       const uint32_t cancelled = NOUVEAU_CANCELLED(dev);
 
@@ -590,7 +592,8 @@ nv30_idx_binding_room(struct nv30_context *nv30, uint64_t copy, unsigned words)
                               "given up after a cancelled kick before them");
          return false;
       }
-      PUSH_SPACE_EX(push, words + 8, 2, 0);
+      if (PUSH_AVAIL(push) < words + 8)
+         PUSH_SPACE_EX(push, words + 8, 2, 0);
    }
    nv30->ps3_idx_bytes = (uint32_t)MIN2(nv30->ps3_idx_bytes + copy, NV30_PS3_IDX_SUBMIT_BYTES);
    return true;
@@ -695,10 +698,15 @@ nv30_draw_elements(struct nv30_context *nv30, bool shorten,
                               "not split (the kernel refuses them)");
       }
 
-      /* the binding and its BEGIN in one submission (a flush between them leaves the batches
-       * through half a binding, which the kernel refuses), within the file's share */
+      /* the whole draw in one submission, as a piece (a flush between the binding and BEGIN
+       * leaves the batches through half a binding, which the kernel refuses; one inside the
+       * primitive makes the kernel copy on to the buffer's end, up to 1 MiB, against this
+       * submission's share), within the file's share. A draw past the cap that couldn't be split
+       * (the kernel refuses it anyway): the binding and BEGIN only */
       if (unlikely(nv30->screen->idx_split) &&
-          !nv30_idx_binding_room(nv30, nv30_idx_copy_bytes((uint64_t)start * isz, count, isz), 5)) {
+          !nv30_idx_binding_room(nv30, nv30_idx_copy_bytes((uint64_t)start * isz, count, isz),
+                                 (uint64_t)count * isz <= NV30_PS3_IDX_PIECE_BYTES ?
+                                 3 + nv30_idx_batch_words(count) : 5)) {
          PUSH_RESET(push, BUFCTX_IDXBUF);
          return;
       }
